From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Subject: [PATCH] luma: windows travel into Grid and back out

Grid hid every window and drew its cards in place in the same frame, and
closing it did the reverse, so both directions were a jump cut. Each card
now starts exactly over its window, with the window's stacking, and
travels to its place in the grid while its name fades in. On leaving,
the cards travel back to their windows, and the chosen window arrives
last and on top before the desktop is handed back. Minimised windows and
windows on other workspaces fade and scale instead of flying. Opening
Grid again while it leaves starts from the desktop, and reduced motion
makes both transitions instant. Emergencies (a system dialog, locking)
still close Grid at once.

--- a/js/ui/lumaGrid.js
+++ b/js/ui/lumaGrid.js
